{
 "name": "voice-message",
 "title": "Voice message",
 "description": "Dictate a message: words appear while you speak and a full pass corrects them when you stop; nothing is sent automatically and your edits are never overwritten. Mistral engines send audio to api.mistral.ai (Voxtral Realtime 3, then Mini Transcribe 3; key only on the server from MISTRAL_API_KEY or Pi's mistral auth.json entry). Local Whisper keeps audio on the server; its first use installs pinned packages from PyPI with enforced hashes and the revision-pinned Whisper small model from huggingface.co, ~900 MB. Engine and language (auto by default) are chosen on the Audio settings page.",
 "tags": [
